.runtime/

# Vite build output. Every file here is generated: `assets/*` is the bundle, and
# `icons/`, `manifest.webmanifest`, `notification-sounds/`, `sw.js` are copied verbatim
# from `frontend/public/`. vite.config sets `emptyOutDir: true`, so nothing hand-authored
# could survive here anyway. Tracking it meant every `npm run build` produced a
# hash-churn diff that dirtied the tree, blocked the automatic fast-forward of the base
# branch, and gave parallel agents meaningless conflicts over generated bundles.
# Packaging does NOT read this: build_desktop.py builds its own copy into
# .runtime/desktop-frontend-build and publishes from there.
# Consequence: a fresh clone or worktree has no UI until you run one `npm run build`
# in `frontend/`. Worktrees never serve the app, so only a fresh clone cares.
src/swe_mux/static/

# === JetBrains IDEs ===
.idea/
*.iml

_agents-orchestrator/
.tmp-orca/
.trash/

# === Test / verification scratch ===
# Throwaway working directories written by live-agent and identity tests and by
# the verification runs. They hold binary mux.db copies and fake executables and
# must never be committed (4f744d8 did, accidentally).
.test-tmp-identity/
test-tmp-codex/
.verify/
# Per-test SQLite files under tests/. The fixture removes them, but a test that
# fails before closing its store leaves one behind (Windows will not unlink a
# file a live connection holds), and those are exactly what got committed before.
tests/.phase2-*.db*
